/li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayajirao-scindia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jayajirao-scindia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jayajirao Scindia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayajirao Scindia was Maharaja of Gwalior from 1843 to 1886.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayakatwang"><span class="enc-name">Jayakatwang</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayakatwang was a ruler of Gelang-gelang in East Java and a descendant of the kings of Kediri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayakeshi-i"><span class="enc-name">Jayakeshi I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayakeshi I was a king of the Kadamba dynasty of Goa in the 11th century, ruling as a feudatory of the Western Chalukya Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayapala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jayapala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jayapala</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayapala was a king of the Hindu Shahi dynasty in the late 10th century, ruling from the Kabul valley to the Punjab.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayapida"><span class="enc-name">Jayapida</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayapida was a king of Kashmir of the Karkota dynasty in the late 8th century, a grandson of Lalitaditya Muktapida.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jayapura"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jayapura.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jayapura</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Jayapura is the capital of the Indonesian province of Papua, on Yos Sudarso Bay on the north coast of New Guinea