ms and the patriotic Finlandia of 1899 made him the leading figure of Finnish music and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-talon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-talon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jean Talon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jean Talon was the first intendant of New France, serving from 1665 to 1668 and from 1670 to 1672 under Louis XIV and his minister Colbert.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-andoche-junot"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-andoche-junot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jean-Andoche Junot</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jean-Andoche Junot was a French general and early comrade of Napoleon Bonaparte.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-bagaza"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-bagaza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jean-Baptiste Bagaza</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jean-Baptiste Bagaza was a Burundian army officer who seized power in a coup in November 1976 and ruled as president until 1987.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jean-Baptiste Colbert</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jean-Baptiste Colbert was a minister of Louis XIV of France who directed finance, commerce and the navy.</span></a></li></ul>
